{/*
  The headless/remote flow — the fifth of the five-diagram family, conforming to the shared
  legend and rendering contract (docs/design/docs-site-visual-blueprint.md §5): hand-authored
  theme-aware inline SVG, colors only from the bound token custom properties
  (--perk-* / --sl-color-*), operational labels IBM Plex Mono 500 at >= 16 CSS px, annotations
  Inter, no animation, nothing hover-only.

  One <figure class="perk-diagram"> wraps two fully-labeled <svg role="img"> variants
  (data-variant="wide", data-variant="narrow" stacked vertical, same reading order); the
  scoped @container query on the figure's inline size (compositions.css makes
  figure.perk-diagram an inline-size container) display:none's exactly one at any width —
  narrow by default, wide only where the content column fits its 736-unit viewBox at scale 1,
  so every label renders at its declared ≥16px size — removing it from rendering AND the
  accessibility tree so a single accessible image is exposed. Browsers without container-query
  support keep the content-identical narrow variant. Each variant carries its own <title> +
  <desc> associated via aria-labelledby (document-unique ids).

  The semantic flow is fixed: the local operator / deterministic supervisor dispatches bounded
  work into a dashed GitHub Actions process boundary holding the implement and address stage
  nodes (the same stage implementation a local run uses); the remote process reads the plan
  and branch from durable GitHub state and writes the pushed PR and reports back to it; the
  durable state leads to a double-outline human gate (review + land) with NO outgoing
  connector — automation stops there. Every connector carries data-from/data-to so the
  post-build checks pin the exact four-edge set (and that no edge originates at human-gate).

  Deliberately static and prop-free: a malformed component fails `astro build`, and the
  post-build structural checks (docs/site/checks/built-site.test.mjs) cover the output.
*/}

<figure class="perk-diagram">
  <svg
    role="img"
    data-variant="wide"
    viewBox="0 0 736 510"
    aria-labelledby="perk-headless-wide-title perk-headless-wide-desc"
  >
    <title id="perk-headless-wide-title">The headless remote flow</title>
    <desc id="perk-headless-wide-desc">
      A local operator or the deterministic supervisor dispatches bounded work into a dashed
      GitHub Actions process boundary containing the implement and address stages — the same
      stage implementation a local run uses. The remote process reads the plan and branch from
      durable GitHub state and writes the pushed pull request, checks, and report comments back
      to it. Durable GitHub state leads to a double-outline HUMAN GATE for review and land,
      which has no automatic outgoing step: automation stops there.
    </desc>
    <g>
      <rect class="node" data-node="operator" x="2" y="8" width="280" height="84" rx="6" />
      <text class="node-label" x="18" y="42">Local operator /</text>
      <text class="node-label" x="18" y="68">deterministic supervisor</text>

      <line class="connector" data-from="operator" data-to="runner" x1="282" y1="50" x2="412" y2="50" />
      <polygon class="arrowhead" points="412,46.5 412,53.5 420,50" />
      <text class="edge-label" x="350" y="36">dispatch</text>

      <rect class="boundary" data-node="runner" x="420" y="8" width="314" height="272" rx="2" />
      <text class="node-label" x="436" y="38">GitHub Actions</text>
      <text class="annotation muted" x="436" y="64">remote process boundary</text>
      <rect class="stage" x="436" y="84" width="210" height="36" rx="6" />
      <text class="node-label" x="452" y="108">○ implement</text>
      <rect class="stage" x="436" y="132" width="210" height="36" rx="6" />
      <text class="node-label" x="452" y="156">○ address</text>
      <text class="annotation muted" x="436" y="212">same stage implementation</text>
      <text class="annotation muted" x="436" y="238">as a local run</text>

      <line class="connector" data-from="github" data-to="runner" x1="480" y1="352" x2="480" y2="288" />
      <polygon class="arrowhead" points="476.5,288 483.5,288 480,280" />
      <text class="edge-label end" x="464" y="322">plan · branch</text>

      <line class="connector" data-from="runner" data-to="github" x1="560" y1="280" x2="560" y2="344" />
      <polygon class="arrowhead" points="556.5,344 563.5,344 560,352" />
      <text class="edge-label start" x="576" y="322">PR · report</text>

      <rect class="artifact" data-node="github" x="420" y="340" width="64" height="26" rx="6" />
      <rect class="artifact" x="420" y="352" width="314" height="150" rx="6" />
      <text class="node-label" x="436" y="384">GitHub state</text>
      <text class="annotation" x="436" y="414">plan issue</text>
      <text class="annotation" x="436" y="442">pushed branch · pull request</text>
      <text class="annotation" x="436" y="470">checks · comments</text>

      <line class="connector" data-from="github" data-to="human-gate" x1="420" y1="407" x2="310" y2="407" />
      <polygon class="arrowhead" points="310,403.5 310,410.5 302,407" />
      <text class="edge-label" x="366" y="393">review</text>

      <rect class="gate-outer" data-node="human-gate" x="2" y="352" width="300" height="110" rx="10" />
      <rect class="gate-inner" x="8" y="358" width="288" height="98" rx="8" />
      <text class="node-label gate-label" x="26" y="398">! HUMAN GATE —</text>
      <text class="node-label gate-label" x="26" y="428">review + land</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <svg
    role="img"
    data-variant="narrow"
    viewBox="0 0 288 796"
    aria-labelledby="perk-headless-narrow-title perk-headless-narrow-desc"
  >
    <title id="perk-headless-narrow-title">The headless remote flow (stacked)</title>
    <desc id="perk-headless-narrow-desc">
      Stacked top to bottom: a local operator or the deterministic supervisor dispatches
      bounded work into a dashed GitHub Actions process boundary containing the implement and
      address stages — the same stage implementation a local run uses. The remote process reads
      the plan and branch from durable GitHub state and writes the pushed pull request, checks,
      and report comments back to it. Durable GitHub state leads to a double-outline HUMAN GATE
      for review and land, which has no automatic outgoing step: automation stops there.
    </desc>
    <g>
      <rect class="node" data-node="operator" x="2" y="8" width="284" height="84" rx="6" />
      <text class="node-label" x="18" y="42">Local operator /</text>
      <text class="node-label" x="18" y="68">deterministic supervisor</text>

      <line class="connector" data-from="operator" data-to="runner" x1="144" y1="92" x2="144" y2="140" />
      <polygon class="arrowhead" points="140.5,140 147.5,140 144,148" />
      <text class="edge-label start" x="162" y="124">dispatch</text>

      <rect class="boundary" data-node="runner" x="2" y="148" width="284" height="244" rx="2" />
      <text class="node-label" x="18" y="178">GitHub Actions</text>
      <text class="annotation muted" x="18" y="204">remote process boundary</text>
      <rect class="stage" x="18" y="222" width="252" height="36" rx="6" />
      <text class="node-label" x="34" y="246">○ implement</text>
      <rect class="stage" x="18" y="270" width="252" height="36" rx="6" />
      <text class="node-label" x="34" y="294">○ address</text>
      <text class="annotation muted" x="18" y="340">same stage implementation</text>
      <text class="annotation muted" x="18" y="366">as a local run</text>

      <line class="connector" data-from="github" data-to="runner" x1="170" y1="478" x2="170" y2="400" />
      <polygon class="arrowhead" points="166.5,400 173.5,400 170,392" />
      <text class="edge-label start" x="184" y="442">plan · branch</text>

      <line class="connector" data-from="runner" data-to="github" x1="118" y1="392" x2="118" y2="470" />
      <polygon class="arrowhead" points="114.5,470 121.5,470 118,478" />
      <text class="edge-label end" x="104" y="442">PR · report</text>

      <rect class="artifact" data-node="github" x="2" y="466" width="64" height="26" rx="6" />
      <rect class="artifact" x="2" y="478" width="284" height="150" rx="6" />
      <text class="node-label" x="18" y="510">GitHub state</text>
      <text class="annotation" x="18" y="540">plan issue</text>
      <text class="annotation" x="18" y="568">pushed branch · pull request</text>
      <text class="annotation" x="18" y="596">checks · comments</text>

      <line class="connector" data-from="github" data-to="human-gate" x1="144" y1="628" x2="144" y2="672" />
      <polygon class="arrowhead" points="140.5,672 147.5,672 144,680" />
      <text class="edge-label start" x="162" y="656">review</text>

      <rect class="gate-outer" data-node="human-gate" x="2" y="680" width="284" height="108" rx="10" />
      <rect class="gate-inner" x="8" y="686" width="272" height="96" rx="8" />
      <text class="node-label gate-label" x="26" y="724">! HUMAN GATE —</text>
      <text class="node-label gate-label" x="26" y="754">review + land</text>
    </g>
  </svg>
</figure>

<style>
  svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
  svg[data-variant="wide"] {
    max-width: 736px;
    display: none;
  }
  svg[data-variant="narrow"] {
    max-width: 288px;
  }
  @container (min-width: 736px) {
    svg[data-variant="wide"] {
      display: block;
    }
    svg[data-variant="narrow"] {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  .node,
  .stage {
    fill: var(--perk-surface);
    stroke: var(--perk-border);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }
  .boundary {
    fill: var(--perk-canvas);
    stroke: var(--perk-border);
    stroke-width: 1;
    stroke-dasharray: 6 4;
  }
  .artifact {
    fill: var(--sl-color-accent-low);
    stroke: var(--perk-border);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }
  .gate-outer {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--perk-warning);
    stroke-width: 2;
  }
  .gate-inner {
    fill: var(--perk-warning-low);
    stroke: var(--perk-warning);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }
  .node-label {
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono), monospace;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 500;
    fill: var(--perk-text);
  }
  .gate-label {
    fill: var(--perk-warning);
  }
  .annotation {
    font-family: var(--sl-font), sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px;
    fill: var(--perk-text);
  }
  .annotation.muted {
    fill: var(--perk-muted);
  }
  .connector {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--perk-muted);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }
  .arrowhead {
    fill: var(--perk-muted);
  }
  .edge-label {
    font-family: var(--sl-font), sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px;
    fill: var(--perk-muted);
    text-anchor: middle;
  }
  .edge-label.start {
    text-anchor: start;
  }
  .edge-label.end {
    text-anchor: end;
  }
</style>
